          <p>Each l represents one canonical verse, with stable numbering and a link to its existing image region. Source verse order and headings are retained. Couplet grouping and canonical line numbers are editorial. A displaced word may remain within its verse with its position marked.</p>
        </segmentation>
        <segmentation>
          <p>Full-page line starts were independently checked on every page. Even lines have the visible ordinary inset. Verse 2 has an additional three-character approximation of the space beside the two-line opening capital; it is not inferred from verse parity.</p>
        </segmentation>
        <correction>
          <p>Uncertain readings remain locally marked with unclear or gap. Observations and uncertainties are documented for a different source reader; ink colour alone does not establish erasure or a separate hand.</p>
        </correction>
